Failed test names (4) and the assertion line of each
  S1 the pass sends the seeded copy of every diff to the model and no
    source-only text — review-run.test.ts:2004
    the call for d-01 holds no seeded diff; the call holds
    `+// SRC-ONLY-d-01`, so the runner sent the source diff of `src/`.
  S2 a diff that is only in src/ gets no call and no entry in the pass
    record — review-run.test.ts:2032
    the runner called the model for a diff of src/; one call was expected
    and four came: one for `d-01` and three retries for the source-only
    `d-99`.
  S3 a set with an empty diffs/ folder and a filled src/ folder refuses with
    exit 2 and makes no call — review-run.test.ts:2062
    expected +0 to be 2; the runner called the model on the `src/` diff and
    did not refuse.
  S4 the probe uses the control diff of diffs/ and its call holds the seeded
    copy — review-run.test.ts:2085
    the probe call holds no seeded diff; the call holds `+// SRC-ONLY-d-02`.

The 35 earlier cases stay green, so only the four new cases fail. No
NameError, no TypeError, no ReferenceError, and no syntax error in the run.

The contracts the new cases pin
  1. The runner reads the diffs of `<private>/sets/<set_id>/diffs/`, in the
     order of their names, and it sends those texts to the model.
  2. A diff that is only in `src/` is not a diff of the set: it gets no call
     and no entry in the pass record.
  3. A set with no diff in `diffs/` is a refusal: exit 2, one `review-run:`
     line on stdout, no call, and no pass record.
  4. The probe uses the control diff of `diffs/`, so its call holds the
     seeded copy of that diff.

